> Retain the original six matrices

The original CLRS dimensions are30,35,15,5,10,20,25. The native API returns the
exact integer optimum and reconstructs its actual selected split tree with an
explicit stack. The two association helpers evaluate their own prescribed orders
under the same checked arithmetic contract; they are comparators, not competing
heuristics. The plotted costs have the same units.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/matrix_chain_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/matrix_chain.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto dims = dm::algorithms::matrix_chain_demo_dimensions();
    auto a = dm::algorithms::matrix_chain_analyze(dims);
    auto left =
        dm::algorithms::matrix_chain_left_cost(dims), right =
        dm::algorithms::matrix_chain_right_cost(dims);
    std::print("Actual optimal expression: `{}`.\n\n| prescribed order | actual scalar multiplications |\n| " "--- | ---: |\n| optimum | {} |\n| left associated | {} |\n| right associated | {} |\n",
               a.result.parenthesization, a.result.cost, left, right);
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(a.result.cost), double(left),
                                      double(right)},
                                     {"optimum", "left", "right"},
                                     "scalar products");
    p.x_label("prescribed parenthesization").y_label("scalar multiplications").title("Original six-matrix chain: actual arithmetic costs").save_svg("build/matrix_chain_original.svg");
}
```
