> Committed subproblems and safe arithmetic

The complete cost and split tables are one-based and filled only above the
diagonal. The next figure groups actual committed interval costs by interval
length; it does not claim costs are monotone for arbitrary dimensions. Each
plotted point comes from a real completed cell after every candidate was
considered.

Dimensions must be positive, including supplied dimensions of an empty chain.
Zero or one dimension denotes no matrices; two dimensions denote one matrix with
zero multiplication cost. Complete table and iteration geometry is checked
before allocation. Costs greater than LLONG_MAX saturate at LLONG_MAX+1 in the
internal/returned table, explicitly represented by an unsigned integer sentinel.
Nonnegative products and sums make saturation order-preserving below this
threshold.

Crucially, an overflowing subproblem need not occur in the chosen full tree. The
planner therefore rejects only an overflowing optimal full-chain cost. It can
still return a representable complete optimum while unused subintervals are
saturated. The ordinary signed result never silently wraps. This differs from
the legacy unchecked signed arithmetic, and invalid nonpositive dimensions now
throw before evaluation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/matrix_chain_cells.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/matrix_chain.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::matrix_chain_trace(dm::algorithms::matrix_chain_demo_dimensions());
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual first matrix | actual last matrix | committed split | committed scalar cost |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.commits) {
        x.push_back(r.j - r.i + 1);
        y.push_back(r.cost);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.i, r.j, r.split, r.cost);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual commits");
    p.x_label("actual interval length in matrices").y_label(
        "actual committed scalar cost").title("Original chain: actual completed interval costs").save_svg("build/matrix_chain_cells.svg");
}
```
