> Exact work and capture

For n matrices, there are n(n−1)/2 nontrivial intervals and n(n−1)(n+1)/6
candidate splits. These are exact loop counts on every input of that length,
giving cubic arithmetic planning time and quadratic table storage. Positive
dimensions do not make the search exponential: the Catalan number counts full
trees, while DP reuses intervals. The explicit reconstruction stack avoids
recursion depth failure; character work is linear in the returned expression
length.

Optional complete trace storage is cubic. Its logical quota counts supplied
dimension scalars, both complete (n+1)-square tables, every actual trial and
every actual commit. Default limit is one million entries; zero disables the
optional cap. Record fields, row headers, capacities, expression bytes and
runtime storage are excluded. Admission checks the complete known loop geometry
before copying or allocation. Quotas are neither byte limits nor wall-clock
guarantees.

For equal dimensions10, every full parenthesization costs1000(n−1). The final
experiment compares actual counts with the closed forms while keeping the
integer cost interpretation explicit.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/matrix_chain_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/matrix_chain.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| matrices n | actual trials | exact cubic formula | actual committed cells | actual " "optimum | equal-dimension formula |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32}) {
        auto a =
            dm::algorithms::matrix_chain_analyze(std::vector<int>(n + 1, 10));
        x.push_back(n);
        y.push_back(a.work.trials);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, a.work.trials,
                   n * (n - 1) * (n + 1) / 6, a.work.cells, a.result.cost,
                   1000 * (n - 1));
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual split trials", {37, 99, 235});
    p.points(x, y, "", {37, 99, 235});
    p.legend({"actual split trials"}, {{37, 99, 235}});
    p.x_label("prescribed matrix count").y_label("actual candidate evaluations").title("Equal-size chains: exact cubic producing work").save_svg("build/matrix_chain_work.svg");
}
```
